-- title:
--   Good points read a place of the Igusa reduction (q=3)
-- statement:
--   The ambient data are as follows. A prime $q$ with $q=3$; a natural number $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Two subfields of $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ occur: $\bar F_{M'}=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-field generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, and $F=$ `fieldBar q M'`, the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ for level $q^2M'$ and $H=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion $\bar F_{M'}\le F$.
--
--   A finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the field over the residue field of $A$ generated by the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j$ expanded at level $M'$) is given, with `hW` saying that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and whose value at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`, the set of supersingular $j$-invariants (those $j$ for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve with invariant $j$ has no non-zero $q$-torsion point).
--
--   Reduction data. `R₀` is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\bar F_{M'}$ to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of $\bar F_{M'}$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the level-$M'$ field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue field, with the scaling and order-transport clauses of that structure. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ lies in $\bar F_{M'}$, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀`-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Likewise `R` is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $F$ to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, with `hR` identifying `R.integers` with `OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O` saying that an element of $\bar F_{M'}$ lies in `R₀.integers` precisely when its image in $F$ lies in `OIg (lineInfty q)`.
--
--   Branch and supersingular valuation rings. A primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an element of `Idx q`) is fixed, together with families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $F$ indexed by the projective line $\mathbf P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. Four hypotheses constrain $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$: `hIg_inf` describes the ring at `lineInfty q` as the Gauss ring, $f\in O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is non-zero and $f\cdot y=x$ after pushing $x,y$ into $\operatorname{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$; `hIg` produces, for every line, a $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` carries `lineInfty q` to that line and for which the ring at the line is the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of $F$ pinned by $\gamma$ and $\zeta$ through the $q$-expansion condition `IsLevelAutBar`, the identity if no such automorphism exists); `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; `hIg_perm` asserts that for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family. Four hypotheses constrain $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$: `hSS_A` says that for each $s\in W$ a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over` says that for $f\in$ `R₀.integers` whose order is non-negative at every place of $\bar F_{M'}$ at which the $q$-expansion of $j$ has non-negative order, and whose `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation ring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in $F$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and, for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value of the `R₀`-residue of $f$ at $s$, the difference between the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is fixed by pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   Arithmetic of the base. An element $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$ is given. A small field of constants $k_0$, an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, is given together with $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, and with the hypotheses that $A\cap k_0$ (the preimage of $A$ in $k_0$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field, and with `hκ`: every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. An auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$ is given, together with $\zeta_0\in k_0$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and $\varpi\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is given with a valuation subring $A_1\subseteq K_1$ cut out by $A$ (i.e. $x\in A_1\iff x\in A$), $A_1$ being a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on $F$ obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to F$, and quantifies over the following further data. First, over an intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ subject to four conditions: the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with $F_0$ is all of $F$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; a regularity condition stating that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every family $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent and every family $a$ of elements of the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K'$ together with $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i\,a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$; and every element of $F$ whose Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K_1$ together with $F_0$. The statement then quantifies over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map agrees with the inclusion of $K_1$ into $F$, over an element $j_1\in T_1$ whose image in $F$ is the element of $\bar F_{M'}$ given by the $q$-expansion $j_q$ of the modular invariant (with $j_1\neq 0$), and over a finset $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from the level-$M'$ field over the residue field of $A$ to that field such that the residue of every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` computed through $R$ equals $j$ applied to its `R₀`-residue, and such that a place $Q$ lies in $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ exactly when there is $s\in W$ with: $g$ lies in the valuation ring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ lies in the valuation ring of $Q$.
--
--   The scheme in play is $\mathfrak X_1=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}=\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ and $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}=\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring of elements integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ and the two chart morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf`. For $x\in\mathfrak X_1$ and $f\in T_1$, the predicate `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of either chart mapping to $x$ there are chart functions $g,h$ with $h\notin y$ and $f\cdot h=g$ in $T_1$; `InMax x f` is the same with the further requirement $g\in y$. `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; for every point $y$ of either chart over $x$, every chart function whose image in $F$ is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in $y$; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ is not a supersingular $j$-invariant, i.e. $\varphi(j_1)\notin$ `ssJSet q Ω`. For a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over the residue field of $A$, the predicate `Reads x Q` says that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation ring of $Q$, and that residue is a non-unit there exactly when `InMax x f` holds. Two further predicates are introduced and do not occur in the conclusion: `Centred P x`, for a place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, requiring $P$ to be rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` to lie in the valuation ring of $P$ with $P$-value in $A$, that value having $A$-valuation less than $1$ exactly when `InMax x f`; and `OffBranch x`, requiring for every line other than `lineInfty q` and every point $y$ of either chart over $x$ a chart function not in $y$ whose image in $F$ is a non-unit of the corresponding $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   The assertion is: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ satisfying `GoodPt x` there exists a place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over the residue field of $A$ with `Reads x Q`.
--
--   This is the existence half of the dictionary between closed points of the two-chart integral model of the full-level modular curve lying on the $\infty$-Igusa branch, away from supersingular $j$-invariants, and places of the reduced Igusa function field, in the case $q=3$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three), where the place so produced is shown to be unique and to avoid the Igusa nodes.
